"""The learned ear on a 60-second upload: does a minute of a record land where the whole preview does?

240 catalogue records, spread across scenes, are cut to their middle 60 seconds at 32 kHz mono (exactly what the site
sends) and read by the reader's own ear code (worker/embed.py, learned_call). Each clip is compared with the record's
place in the catalogue's ear (data/walk_ear.json, from the full previews): the rank of the record itself among every
record in the ear, the cosine between the two, and how many of the clip's ten nearest neighbours are the full
preview's. Results arrive as run annotations.   modal run worker/ear_upload_test.py
"""
